.quarto/
*_cache/
*_files/
*.log
*.aux
*.out

# renv specific
# Keep the lockfile and activation scripts, but ignore the library itself
renv/library/
renv/python/
renv/staging/
!renv/activate.R
!renv/settings.json

# Third-party RAW datasets too large to redistribute (multi-GB, and
# several sources restrict redistribution in their own terms of use --
# GADM, EOG). These paths are local symlinks back to the main
# repository's data/ folder for this developer's own machine -- see
# README.md, "What's physically shipped vs. symlinked", for the
# download link for each. A fresh clone won't have these symlinks at
# all since they're ignored here, not committed as broken links.
#
# This project's OWN derived outputs of comparable size (analysis_panel.csv,
# the harmonized panel, gadm_holepunched_adm1.gpkg, etc.) are NOT excluded
# here -- they're tracked via Git LFS instead (see .gitattributes), since
# redistributing this project's own computed data carries none of that
# licensing risk, and shipping them is what lets `make analysis` run
# end-to-end with zero downloads. See README.md, "Quickstart".
01_datasets/raw/gadm_3.6/
# No trailing slash on these two: they are symlinks (not real
# directories) on this developer's machine, pointing outside the repo
# to the main repository's own data/ folder -- a directory-only
# gitignore pattern (trailing /) does not match a symlink, so the
# untrailed form is needed to actually exclude them.
01_datasets/raw/dmsp_raster_eog_manual
01_datasets/raw/viirs_raster_eog_manual

# Not present on disk when this package was built, so not sized/copied
# above -- but 01_download_gadm.R (Stage 01) downloads this GADM 4.1
# "all levels" archive fresh on a real run, and it is large (~1-2GB).
# Pre-ignoring it here stops a future Stage 01 run from silently growing
# this package past GitHub-friendly size.
01_datasets/raw/gadm_4.1/global/gadm_410-levels.zip
01_datasets/raw/gadm_4.1/global/gadm_410-levels/

# Decompressed at runtime from the shipped .gz by ensure_decompressed()
# (utils.R) -- not re-committed, the .gz alone is the tracked source.
01_datasets/processed/grid_cells_50km.gpkg
01_datasets/processed/grid_cells_100km.gpkg
01_datasets/processed/grid_cells_200km.gpkg
01_datasets/processed/grid_cells_400km.gpkg
01_datasets/processed/analysis_panel.csv
01_datasets/processed/gadm_holepunched_adm1.gpkg
01_datasets/processed/population_adm2.csv
01_datasets/processed/population_adm2_ghspop_interpolated.csv
01_datasets/processed/ntl/harmonized_dmsp_viirs_adm2_panel.csv
01_datasets/raw/qog/qog_std_ts_jan26.csv

# Fitted-model .rds files from Stages 28/36-39: regenerated fresh by
# `make core` / `make supplementary` and not committed. One of these
# (Stage 28's grid models) is a completely dead output nothing
# downstream ever reads; the other four ARE read directly by
# supplementary.qmd's tables, but only when you re-render from source
# after running the pipeline yourself -- since 04_paper/ ships its PDF and
# HTML already built, a normal read of the paper needs none of these.
# All five are 75MB-3GB and were found sitting in an earlier, unrelated
# repository's history without ever having been added to Git LFS.
01_datasets/processed/ntl/table4_col4_7_grid_models_hrsample.rds
01_datasets/processed/ntl/table3_dynamics_models.rds
01_datasets/processed/ntl/table5_determinants_models.rds
01_datasets/processed/ntl/table6_continents_models.rds
01_datasets/processed/ntl/table7_aid_oil_models.rds
